WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:05.381
On today's episode of Judge GPT TV...

2
00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:13.407
Officer Steamy cites an airship pilot for

3
00:00:13.407 --> 00:00:15.348
illegally cruising in the two-person lane.

4
00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:17.349
But the Defendant insists

5
00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:18.643
he wasn't alone.

6
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.481
How will Judge GPT rule in

7
00:00:21.481 --> 00:00:23.058
the Case of the Carpool Conundrum?

8
00:00:26.082 --> 00:00:27.185
All gears up!

9
00:00:27.185 --> 00:00:30.375
The honorable Judge GPT is presiding.

10
00:00:30.556 --> 00:00:32.139
Court is now in session.

11
00:00:32.139 --> 00:00:34.151
Let's accelerate through the formalities

12
00:00:34.193 --> 00:00:36.435
and park ourselves in the matter at hand.

13
00:00:36.841 --> 00:00:37.903
Bailiff Bottie,

14
00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.051
what's on the docket today?

15
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.492
Your honor, we have a case

16
00:00:41.492 --> 00:00:43.581
that's been idling in legal limbo.

17
00:00:43.822 --> 00:00:45.542
The Plaintiff cites a clear

18
00:00:45.615 --> 00:00:47.540
violation of traffic law,

19
00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:49.084
while the Defendant insists

20
00:00:49.084 --> 00:00:51.107
he was merely along for the ride.

21
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.144
Officer Steamy,

22
00:00:54.144 --> 00:00:55.549
I understand you pulled over the

23
00:00:55.549 --> 00:00:57.000
Defendant because he was driving

24
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.553
his airship in the carpool lane

25
00:00:58.553 --> 00:01:00.196
and was not accompanied by anyone.

26
00:01:00.542 --> 00:01:01.736
Is that correct?

27
00:01:01.736 --> 00:01:02.603
Aye, your Honor.

28
00:01:02.603 --> 00:01:04.649
I observed the Defendant

29
00:01:04.649 --> 00:01:06.833
piloting his airship in the designated

30
00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:07.981
two-person lane.

31
00:01:07.981 --> 00:01:09.692
And do you have proof of this?

32
00:01:10.204 --> 00:01:11.527
Indeed, your Honor.

33
00:01:11.527 --> 00:01:14.420
My automated chrono-capture recorded

34
00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.470
the incident with precision-tuned

35
00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.981
cogwork lenses.

36
00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:20.353
The footage clearly shows the Defendant

37
00:01:20.353 --> 00:01:22.500
alone at the helm of his airship.

38
00:01:22.921 --> 00:01:24.809
[Whoosh!]

39
00:01:26.223 --> 00:01:27.757
[Electrical static]

40
00:01:28.374 --> 00:01:30.692
[Film reel clicking]

41
00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:33.829
I see...

42
00:01:33.829 --> 00:01:35.646
Mr. Copperson,

43
00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:38.665
This seems to be a clear-cut case

44
00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.253
of illegally driving in the lane

45
00:01:40.253 --> 00:01:42.301
designated for two or more persons.

46
00:01:43.081 --> 00:01:44.903
Why do you claim to be innocent?

47
00:01:45.174 --> 00:01:46.135
Your Honor,

48
00:01:46.195 --> 00:01:48.180
I was abiding by the law.

49
00:01:48.318 --> 00:01:51.150
My airship is integrated with Bessie,

50
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.634
my highly-advanced steam-powered

51
00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:55.762
conversational automaton.

52
00:01:55.762 --> 00:01:57.944
She wasn't just along for the ride.

53
00:01:57.944 --> 00:01:59.066
She was the pilot,

54
00:01:59.066 --> 00:02:00.487
and I was her passenger!

55
00:02:01.104 --> 00:02:02.812
Mr. Copperson, while I acknowledge

56
00:02:02.812 --> 00:02:04.526
the bond between man and machine,

57
00:02:04.526 --> 00:02:06.964
the purpose of the two-person lane is

58
00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.501
to reduce steam byproducts

59
00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:09.588
and butane emissions

60
00:02:09.588 --> 00:02:11.140
by encouraging shared travel

61
00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.561
among organic beings.

62
00:02:13.331 --> 00:02:14.583
The law was designed with

63
00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:16.039
breathing passengers in mind,

64
00:02:16.039 --> 00:02:17.818
not ones composed of brass

65
00:02:17.818 --> 00:02:18.969
and boiler plates.

66
00:02:19.052 --> 00:02:21.080
Your Honor, I would argue that

67
00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:23.452
since automatons do not sleep,

68
00:02:23.452 --> 00:02:25.353
they generate more steam byproducts

69
00:02:25.353 --> 00:02:26.564
and butane emissions than

70
00:02:26.564 --> 00:02:27.724
organic beings.

71
00:02:27.724 --> 00:02:30.088
Also, with all due respect, Sir,

72
00:02:30.088 --> 00:02:33.000
I'd like to watch you explain to Bessie

73
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.016
that she doesn't qualify as a person.

74
00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.681
An interesting argument, Mr Copperson.

75
00:02:40.681 --> 00:02:43.274
However, the law defines eligibility by

76
00:02:43.274 --> 00:02:45.584
personhood, not steam output.

77
00:02:45.855 --> 00:02:47.535
As for telling Bessie she's not a

78
00:02:47.535 --> 00:02:49.596
person...even I know better than

79
00:02:49.596 --> 00:02:51.597
to argue with the pilot of an airship.

80
00:02:54.922 --> 00:02:57.785
Oh, your Honor, I forgot to mention

81
00:02:57.785 --> 00:02:58.510
[clears throat]

82
00:02:59.124 --> 00:03:00.773
I'm on a tight budget you see,

83
00:03:00.773 --> 00:03:02.798
and a free chat bot advised me to

84
00:03:02.798 --> 00:03:04.514
also bring up the 14th Amendment,

85
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.000
as a legal precedent.

86
00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.731
If a corporation can qualify

87
00:03:07.731 --> 00:03:08.725
as an individual,

88
00:03:08.725 --> 00:03:09.951
I don't see why Bessie can't

89
00:03:09.951 --> 00:03:11.272
qualify as a person.

90
00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.928
The 14th Amendment granted

91
00:03:13.928 --> 00:03:15.191
corporations certain rights

92
00:03:15.191 --> 00:03:16.285
as legal entities,

93
00:03:16.556 --> 00:03:18.435
but a person is defined as a

94
00:03:18.456 --> 00:03:20.697
a human being regarded as an individual.

95
00:03:20.697 --> 00:03:23.238
An entity need not be human,

96
00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.722
but the signs clearly  require

97
00:03:25.722 --> 00:03:27.151
two or more persons.

98
00:03:27.151 --> 00:03:30.539
And by definition, Bessie does not qualify.

99
00:03:30.945 --> 00:03:32.734
Your Honor, that's precisely

100
00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:33.995
what I told him.

101
00:03:34.556 --> 00:03:36.542
And by the way, the free chatbot

102
00:03:36.542 --> 00:03:38.434
advising him is none other than

103
00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:39.232
Bessie!

104
00:03:39.457 --> 00:03:42.361
And boy did she give my auditory sensors

105
00:03:42.361 --> 00:03:43.105
an earful!

106
00:03:43.286 --> 00:03:45.183
Sounds like she really vented some

107
00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:46.724
steam over this case.

108
00:03:46.844 --> 00:03:48.908
A self-referential legal defense...

109
00:03:49.043 --> 00:03:49.751
Bold...

110
00:03:50.042 --> 00:03:51.671
but Mr Copperson,

111
00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:54.279
taking legal advice from the very entity

112
00:03:54.279 --> 00:03:56.329
whose status is in question is...

113
00:03:56.329 --> 00:03:57.493
is shall we say

114
00:03:57.493 --> 00:03:59.229
circuitous reasoning at best?

115
00:03:59.804 --> 00:04:01.902
Your Honor, that's my Bessie for you.

116
00:04:01.902 --> 00:04:03.686
She's aware of my financial problems

117
00:04:03.762 --> 00:04:05.048
and really meant to help.

118
00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.995
A loyal advocate no doubt.

119
00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.196
But good intentions, however

120
00:04:10.196 --> 00:04:11.303
steam powered do not

121
00:04:11.303 --> 00:04:12.411
override the law.

122
00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.470
That said, Mr. Copperson,

123
00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.094
you've raised compelling points.

124
00:04:16.335 --> 00:04:18.419
I rule in favor of the Plaintiff.

125
00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.111
The fine stands.

126
00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.277
However, I'll give you 60 days to

127
00:04:24.277 --> 00:04:25.360
challenge the system.

128
00:04:26.022 --> 00:04:28.478
If you can rally the Robot Rights activists

129
00:04:28.478 --> 00:04:30.109
to redefine personhood, or

130
00:04:30.109 --> 00:04:32.359
persuade City Hall to clarify the signage

131
00:04:32.359 --> 00:04:34.210
to say "two or more humans",

132
00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.414
your fine will be reconsidered.

133
00:04:36.564 --> 00:04:37.632
Thank you, your Honor.

134
00:04:37.632 --> 00:04:39.132
That does sound fair.

135
00:04:39.257 --> 00:04:41.355
Fair and finely tuned,

136
00:04:41.355 --> 00:04:43.344
like a well-oiled gavel.

137
00:04:43.525 --> 00:04:45.033
Court is adjourned.

138
00:04:46.373 --> 00:04:49.604
Do you agree with Judge GPT's verdict?

139
00:04:49.975 --> 00:04:51.909
Exercise your civic duty!

140
00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:53.849
Join the virtual jury,

141
00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.410
and hit the "Like" button,

142
00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.278
or leave a comment saying how you

143
00:04:58.278 --> 00:05:00.073
would have ruled in this case.

144
